### API Request 3: Callouts Report Fetch (Success Verification)
*   **Endpoint:** `/call_out` (Query: `start=2026-10-25&end=2026-10-31`)
*   **Trigger Action:** Navigated to Daily Reports -> Callouts Report and selected the "Last Week" date filter.
*   **Response Status:** `200 OK`
*   **Date-Filter Parameter Check:** **PASSED.** 
    *   *Observation:* The frontend successfully requests data for the week of Oct 25 - Oct 31. The backend honors the date bound, returning items stamped precisely with `"date": "2026-10-25T00:00:00.000Z"`.
*   **Data Consistency Check:** **PASSED.**
    *   *Observation:* The API payload directly populates the visible frontend columns. For instance, the JSON object contains `"name": "Alejandro Cortes Alvarado"`, `"callout_time": "Call Out - Day Before"`, and `"excused": "No"`, which matches the rendered UI table row identically.
*   **Evidence Attachments:**
    *   ![Callouts Report UI and Network](image_285e59.png)
*   **Practical Assertions (Postman/Chai format):**
    ```javascript
    pm.test("Status code is 200", function () {
        pm.response.to.have.status(200);
    });
    pm.test("Response successfully fetches CallOut data", function () {
        var jsonData = pm.response.json();
        pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;
        pm.expect(jsonData.message).to.equal("CallOut data fetched successfully");
    });
    pm.test("Data metrics contain valid Callout properties", function () {
        var jsonData = pm.response.json();
        if (jsonData.data.length > 0) {
            pm.expect(jsonData.data[0].metrics).to.have.property('name');
            pm.expect(jsonData.data[0].metrics).to.have.property('callout_time');
            pm.expect(jsonData.data[0].metrics).to.have.property('excused');
        }
    });
    ```
